{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And you shall not turn aside from all the words</b> — this continues from <b>when you heed</b> (Deuteronomy 28:13), the meaning being: all these blessings shall come upon you when you heed His commandments and when you do not turn right or left from all the words that I command you — in the matter of idolatry. For if you go after other elohim to serve them, you have already turned aside from all His commandments, and there is no desire whatsoever in any commandment you may perform. And this is not as the words of Baal ha-Halakhot, who counted it as a negative commandment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Baal ha-Halakhot refers to the author of the Sefer Mitzvot Gadol; Ramban disputes counting this verse as an independent negative commandment."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:29.737379366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}